    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0264" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg176"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Desprez to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the French Republic in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1892-09-27"><hi rendition="#italic">September
                                27, 1892</hi></date>. (Received September 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>:</p>
                <p>In a letter dated 27th of August last, Mr. Alvey A. Adee communicated to me the
                    copy of a telegram that you were kind enough to address to Mr. Patenôtre on
                    board of the <hi rendition="#italic">Bretagne</hi> to inform him of the
                    dismissal of the policeman, who, on the 30th of May last, in the town of
                    Jeannette, Pa., tore the French flags placed by one of our countrymen in the
                    window of his house.</p>
                <p>I am instructed by the minister of foreign affairs to acquaint you that the
                    French Government appreciates the satisfaction accorded it in this case by the
                    Federal Government, at the request of Mr. Patenôtre.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Desprez.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
